module gunbc.census_memo_seed_growth

import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// FORWARD-FREEZE RECEIPT for the hand Rust in the cost path of one host builtin. Authored
// because gunbc.seed_growth_admission seed_growth_forward_freeze_policy_note makes
// unenumerated hand growth in src/v1 a stop-line. Requested by review 56854 on gunbc#9428;
// RE-SCOPED 2026-10-21 when the MEMO this receipt was written for was DELETED. The module and
// data keep their names because five sibling receipts and src/v2/workflow/required_floor.dag
// cite them as prose authority -- renaming would orphan those citations for a cosmetic gain, so
// the truth lives in this header instead (§4b: declare the deficit, do not conceal it).
//
// THE HAND-OVER, plainly, so the roster does not carry a monument to deleted code. This receipt
// once enumerated `compile_dag_diagnostic_census_memo_counts` and
// `compile_dag_diagnostic_census_uncached` -- the two hand items that memoized the census. BOTH
// ARE GONE. What replaces them answers the SAME question (a census call must not pay for the
// whole corpus again for work a prior call in the same process already did), by READING THROUGH
// shared process-level state instead of asserting a cached answer, and that replacement's two
// reporting functions are the hand growth enumerated below.
//
// WHY THE MEMO WAS DELETED AND NOT RE-PAIRED. It was never arbitrary caching: it repaired a
// measured cost-shape defect (the sibling compile_dag_rust_emit_check was memoized and this was
// not, so a witness asking two QUESTIONS about one source paid two full compiles; the row
// reached 5437ms CPU against the then-standing 5000ms claim CPU refusal -- the admissible repair
// being to stop recomputing, never to raise the line). But its soundness precondition was the
// floor's prepared-inventory snapshot: it keyed on the source TOGETHER WITH that inventory's
// content digest, because build_module_path_index_from_witness_roots reads those bytes and the
// census is a function of the corpus as well as the source. When run_required_floor was deleted
// the guard could never arm, every call fell through to disk, and what remained was a HashMap
// monument plus two atomics reporting (0, 0) forever -- a cache that cached nothing, with a hit
// rate no one could disprove because nothing read it. Re-arming it would require declaring every
// input the census now reads (corpus bytes, and the process-level cache state it borrows), a
// stronger claim than anything here can establish; DESIGN's cache-impurity rule forbids a hit
// that asserts disk. So the recomputation is DELETED at its sources rather than papered over.
//
// THE COST, BY EXECUTION NOT ARGUMENT. A warm census call measured 12.9 s before this change and
// 0.34 s after, and census_cost_step0_measurement now REFUSES the series when a corpus module-path
// index materializes at all (its gate is INDEX_CLONES == 0 over warm calls). Where the memo made
// the repeat call free by asserting a fact about disk, these make it cheap by not doing the work.
//
// WHY THE INSTRUMENTS ARE RUST AND NOT .dag, which is the question this receipt exists to answer
// honestly. The instrumented SUBJECT is a host builtin: compile_dag_diagnostic_census runs
// v1_compiler_compile compile_sources synchronously in the seed, and the substrate has no
// representation of it to attach a counter to. A .dag-side instrument would have to key on a
// compile the substrate cannot name, which is a layer inversion rather than a migration -- the
// same boundary gunbc.claim_unwind_seed_growth records one seam over. So the reporting stays
// co-located with the builtin it reports on, exactly where the deleted memo sat.
//
// WHAT IS NOT NETTED. compile_dag_diagnostic_census itself is ExistingSeedItemModified per
// gunbc.seed_growth_admission SeedGrowthChangeDisposition -- it keeps its name, its signature and
// its builtin spelling; its former memoized wrapper and the _uncached split collapsed into it (a
// wrapper that only forwards is authored duplication, DESIGN section 3; the sibling keeps its
// split for a reason this one never had -- its _uncached returns EmitCheckRead, a different type).
//
// HAND-ITEM DELTA: +2 citable declarations, both in v1_compiler.cli_run.emit_host, both
// reporting-only. The six counters they read are module-level statics and are NOT citable
// declarations; they are named here rather than omitted, because a receipt that counts only what
// the roster can cite would under-report its own growth.
data census_memo_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.emit_host", decl_name: "compile_dag_diagnostic_census_memo_counts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.emit_host", decl_name: "compile_dag_diagnostic_census_uncached", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "Reporting on a host builtin's cost path is a property of the host that runs it. compile_dag_diagnostic_census_cost_counts reads the six counters at the seams where a census call can pay for the corpus (the module-path index entry, the scratch's source-file map, every real disk read the resolve path performs); reset_compile_dag_diagnostic_census_cost_counts brackets a call series so the reading is a process-differential DELTA, never a claim about another process. Neither decides anything: the census vocabulary is unchanged and pre-existing, no verdict branches on them, and the severity policy stays in compile_clean_diagnostic_is_hard.\n\nENUMERATED RATHER THAN COUNTED. Both are free functions, so the citable count and the real count are both two; nothing lands in seed_growth_uncitable_item_keys. The six statics they read are not declarations and are disclosed in this file's header instead.\n\nWHY A COUNTER AND NOT A MEMO IS THE HAND HALF NOW. A memo asserts a result; a counter only states what was touched. The deleted memo needed a content key complete over every input the census reads -- the claim the floor snapshot used to supply and nothing supplies now -- while a counter needs only that the seam it sits on is the seam the cost goes through, and THAT is checked rather than asserted: census_cost_step0_measurement refuses the series when the corpus-index clone count is nonzero over warm calls, so the gate cannot be turned green by a dead counter, because the same series asserts the surviving disk-read counter is nonzero (a counter mechanism that stopped seeing work would make the zero decoration, not cost).",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete both when compile_dag_diagnostic_census and its sibling compile_dag_rust_emit_check are MODELED operations rather than host builtins -- at which point their sharing is the substrate's own Realization memoization on a content hash (DESIGN section 2, one kernel spanning resolve-cost to sccache), the corpus state they read through is a modeled node the cost model already sees, and hand-carried counters beside them are exactly the duplicated authority that carrier dissolves. The two siblings migrate together or not at all: leaving one hand-instrumented beside a modeled sibling would be the fork this receipt's own single-authority argument refuses. NOTE FOR THE READER OF 2026-10-21: the trigger has NOT fired. What fired was the DELETION of the memo the trigger had been written against, because that memo lost its soundness precondition (see the header); the census is still a host builtin dispatched by the interpreter, so the enumerated items are live and this row stays.",
  current_boundary: "Confined to one builtin and one process. The counters are read only by census_cost_step0_measurement and reset only by its own call; no verdict anywhere branches on them, and no caller outside the census path sees them. The sharing they measure is READ-ONLY: a census call reads the process-shared index and writes only into a scratch holding the fixture's own sources, so the shared index is never populated with fixture state -- proved by fixture_closure_extension_does_not_populate_the_process_shared_index (green) against fixture_closure_extension_via_shared_index_grows_both_closure_edges (the pre-fix route, which still reproduces the leak); and the pool caches a scratch reads through are pool facts, checked by this file's companion measurement's collision fixture (a fixture named over a pool module leaves the census digest byte-identical). The census output itself is asserted byte-identical to the pre-change digest (23 rows), so the cost path changed and the reported content did not. THE ATTRIBUTION THAT MOVED WITH THE MEMO, declared rather than hidden: record_shared_artifact_fill_cpu was written on this builtin's memo MISS, and that call is gone with the memo -- no census path writes the fill accumulator any more (only the decl_facts census in coproduct_reflection does). That is not a dropped attribution but a vanished one: the shared construction the memo used to bracket and charge is now a first-touch inside the ordinary compile, charged the way any other compile is. If a future reader wants the census's shared-build cost attributed on its own clock again, that is the capability this deletion removed, and the counters are where it would be re-instrumented -- not a re-armed memo."
}
